#question(title: [The original sequence defined by recurrence -- done right])[
  Consider the sequence
  $display({R_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ defined by
  $
    cases( & quad R_0 = 1, forall n in NN comma quad & quad R_(n + 1) = frac(R_n + 2, R_n + 3))
  $

  + Prove $display({R_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ is
    bounded below by 0.
  + Prove $display({R_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ is
    decreasing (use induction)
  + Prove $display({R_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ is
    convergent (use a theorem)
  + Now the calculation in the earlier slide
    is correct, and we can get the value of
    the limit.
]
